00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:07,047
Got it.

72
00:05:07,047 --> 00:05:09,798
What do I need to remember?

73
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:17,563
A milestone groups issues/PRs toward a goal, usually a release, with progress and a due date.

74
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:25,510
Create and inspect with gh api …/milestones; assign with --milestone TITLE.

75
00:05:26,067 --> 00:05:28,606
Titles must match exactly.

76
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:32,596
Why would I need projects?

77
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:39,650
GitHub Projects are planning boards and tables built on top of issues and pull requests,

78
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:42,019
across one or many repositories:

79
00:05:42,019 --> 00:05:49,424
columns such as Todo / In progress / Done, custom fields (priority, estimate, iteration), and views.

80
00:05:49,424 --> 00:05:54,163
They do not change Git at all; they organise the work around it.

81
00:05:55,900 --> 00:06:00,300
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

82
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:08,673
With the project scope (see "Fix" below), create a project, add an issue, and move it across the board:

83
00:06:10,433 --> 00:06:11,886
Let me try something.

84
00:06:11,886 --> 00:06:19,703
Use the project commands with a token that was created without the project scope (the default for gh auth login):

85
00:06:20,267 --> 00:06:25,243
your authentication token is missing required scopes [read:project]:

86
00:06:25,243 --> 00:06:30,365
OAuth tokens carry scopes, the list of things they may do (lesson 48).

87
00:06:30,365 --> 00:06:35,707
repo covers code, issues and PRs, but Projects are a separate permission,

88
00:06:35,707 --> 00:06:40,684
so the same token that pushes and opens issues cannot read projects.

89
00:06:40,684 --> 00:06:44,196
GitHub tells you exactly which scope is missing.

90
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:50,873
Grant the scope (opens the browser to confirm), then retry:

91
00:06:52,633 --> 00:06:53,347
Got it.

92
00:06:53,347 --> 00:06:56,098
What do I need to remember?

93
00:06:56,633 --> 00:07:04,028
Projects organise issues and PRs into boards, tables and roadmaps, across repositories.

94
00:07:04,567 --> 00:07:09,320
The CLI needs the project (or read:project) scope:

95
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:11,886
gh auth refresh -s project.

96
00:07:12,433 --> 00:07:17,828
Project workflows keep the board in sync with issue and PR states automatically.

97
00:07:19,567 --> 00:07:22,101
What should I know about releases?

98
00:07:22,667 --> 00:07:27,597
A GitHub Release is a tag (lesson 68) plus a page:

99
00:07:27,597 --> 00:07:35,191
title, release notes, and downloadable files (binaries, archives, checksums).

100
