122
00:09:16,647 --> 00:09:19,398
What do I need to remember?

123
00:09:19,933 --> 00:09:26,393
Release = tag + notes + assets; versions follow MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH.

124
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:34,248
gh release create/list/view/edit/delete; --generate-notes for automatic notes.

125
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:38,180
Never reuse a version for different content:

126
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:40,715
edit notes, release new versions.

127
00:09:42,467 --> 00:09:45,706
Can you show me GitHub Actions introduction?

128
00:09:46,267 --> 00:09:48,968
How Git events start automation:

129
00:09:48,968 --> 00:09:57,155
a push or a pull request triggers a workflow defined in the repository (.github/workflows/*.yml),

130
00:09:57,155 --> 00:10:00,363
and GitHub runs it on a fresh machine.

131
00:10:00,363 --> 00:10:04,077
This lesson is the bridge from Git to CI/CD:

132
00:10:04,077 --> 00:10:08,044
one small workflow, a failing run, and the fix.

133
00:10:08,044 --> 00:10:15,641
GitHub Actions itself (jobs, matrices, secrets, OIDC, deployments) is a course of its own.

134
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:21,799
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

135
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:31,543
A workflow that checks every line of prices.csv (lesson 97 turned prices into CSV) has a name and a number:

136
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,907
The push started a run.

137
00:10:33,907 --> 00:10:39,879
Wait for it (GitHub needs a few seconds to register it) and show the result:

138
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,366
Let me try something.

139
00:10:43,366 --> 00:10:45,925
A careless edit pushed to main:

140
00:10:45,925 --> 00:10:47,988
a price without decimals.

141
00:10:48,533 --> 00:10:51,166
The commit shows a red ✗ on GitHub.

142
00:10:51,166 --> 00:10:54,853
The failed step's log says exactly what is wrong:

143
00:10:56,600 --> 00:11:00,784
